{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791737054,"nonce":"8xWLnw4X2VM1xaMi1kd7qgOKVxE=","title":"Cranelift boxes every argument on ordinary interface calls","message":"A nongeneric TickInterface.tick(Int):Void call allocates 48 bytes per invocation in Cranelift while concrete/base-class calls and the same interface call in interpreter or LLVM allocate zero. This prevents interface-based per-frame coordinators from satisfying zero-allocation checks during hybrid execution.\n\nEngine-independent reproducer: /Users/amaterasu/Vibranium/chimpmonk/repro/ash_interface_alloc/Repro.hx and README.md. Compile with haxe -cp \u003crepro-directory\u003e -main Repro -hl /tmp/interface.hl; run with ASH_GC_TLAB=0 for precise GC accounting. The probe retains an extracted method and checks the final counter equals 230912, ensuring dispatch behavior is preserved. No SIMD, fibers or engine dependency is needed.\n\nRechecked on local Ash release 0.1.5, SHA256 161234e0b500c064541be3aeb756941b72a6c0b0bacf3f028283a5f4bdf26fcd, Ash source HEAD 2b989697. Each tier ran sequentially through ChimpMonk's scripts/bench.py with 512 MiB RSS and 30-second limits; sampled peaks up to 72.4 MiB. Exact allocation results for the least of seven 8192-operation windows:\n- Cranelift JIT: interface 393216 bytes (48/call); method extraction 262144 (32/read); concrete/base/cached invocation zero.\n- LLVM JIT: interface zero; method extraction 262144; concrete/base/cached invocation zero.\n- Interpreter: same as LLVM.\n- Default hybrid --preset game: interface 215040 bytes during tier transitions; method extraction 262144; concrete/base/cached invocation zero. Hybrid amounts depend on promotion timing; the pinned-tier controls isolate the issue.\n\nReading a bound method legitimately materializes a closure in every tier; that is a control, not the reported defect. Static source inspection points to crates/ash/src/cranelift/codegen.rs emit_virtual_call: every nonempty tail allocates an HDYN varray using alloc_dyn_array_helper and boxes each argument with box_dynamic/hlp_make_dyn before calling hlp_vcall_dyn. For this one-Int argument the 32-byte varray and 16-byte box account for the measured 48 bytes. LLVM's virtual-slot direct path avoids this when the resolved signature matches; Cranelift currently always uses the boxed marshalling path.\n\nRequest: an ABI-checked direct fast path for matching interface/implementation signatures, or an equivalent nonallocating marshaller. Keep safe dynamic fallback for generic specialization, absent virtual slots, casts, bound method extraction, return adaptation and exception behavior. Do not assume the interface's static ABI matches a generic implementation: preserve the fixes exercised by 0a11f3d and 0b77b7d. Tests should cover Int/Void as here, Single and Dynamic-returning generic implementations, mutable/reloaded targets, and throwing methods.\n\nAcceptance: this interface call allocates zero in pinned Cranelift and warmed hybrid; counter/result behavior remains correct; meaningful generic ABI and exception tests pass. No Ash source has been changed by this investigation. Details and initial scene impact are also recorded on ChimpMonk eb9a63d. Related accurate GC counters: 7e9d728.\n\nRaw guarded control results:\n[\n  {\n    \"tier\": \"cranelift\",\n    \"load\": [\n      5.50830078125,\n      12.9560546875,\n      40.44921875\n    ],\n    \"log\": \"/var/folders/t0/90bythzn6f11s52g5z84fnpm0000gn/T/chimpmonk-benchmark-tlur7d_v.log\",\n    \"result\": {\n      \"base\": 0,\n      \"cachedCall\": 0,\n      \"calls\": 8192,\n      \"direct\": 0,\n      \"readMethod\": 262144,\n      \"total\": 230912,\n      \"viaInterface\": 393216\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"tier\": \"llvm\",\n    \"load\": [\n      5.50830078125,\n      12.9560546875,\n      40.44921875\n    ],\n    \"log\": \"/var/folders/t0/90bythzn6f11s52g5z84fnpm0000gn/T/chimpmonk-benchmark-hwtnwafj.log\",\n    \"result\": {\n      \"base\": 0,\n      \"cachedCall\": 0,\n      \"calls\": 8192,\n      \"direct\": 0,\n      \"readMethod\": 262144,\n      \"total\": 230912,\n      \"viaInterface\": 0\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"tier\": \"interp\",\n    \"load\": [\n      5.22705078125,\n      12.77392578125,\n      40.2236328125\n    ],\n    \"log\": \"/var/folders/t0/90bythzn6f11s52g5z84fnpm0000gn/T/chimpmonk-benchmark-jx7l2m0o.log\",\n    \"result\": {\n      \"base\": 0,\n      \"cachedCall\": 0,\n      \"calls\": 8192,\n      \"direct\": 0,\n      \"readMethod\": 262144,\n      \"total\": 230912,\n      \"viaInterface\": 0\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"tier\": \"hybrid\",\n    \"load\": [\n      5.22705078125,\n      12.77392578125,\n      40.2236328125\n    ],\n    \"log\": \"/var/folders/t0/90bythzn6f11s52g5z84fnpm0000gn/T/chimpmonk-benchmark-ekzvh02o.log\",\n    \"result\": {\n      \"base\": 0,\n      \"cachedCall\": 0,\n      \"calls\": 8192,\n      \"direct\": 0,\n      \"readMethod\": 262144,\n      \"total\": 230912,\n      \"viaInterface\": 215040\n    }\n  }\n]","files":null}]}